 "notes": "Regular grid, heavily corrected with paste-on slips (some slips overhang the street lines; centres taken from the underlying block lines and water-pipe lines). The sheet is rotated very slightly: east-west streets rise ~15 px from west to east. Streets print without suffixes (BOONE, MAY, KENTON, CONCORD, WAYNE, MORGAN, BURBANK, WILKINSON, HEMLOCK); McMillan prints 'E. McMILLAN'. North of McMillan is Volume 4: the leg opposite May is an unnamed street on this sheet (its centre ~20 px west of May's, x~1566), and HEMLOCK enters from the north as a T between Kenton and Concord. Boone, Kenton and Concord stop at McMillan (T from the south). The 20 ft alley one block south of McMillan is printed 'LINDSAY (KEMPER)' west of May (Kemper being a pasted correction) and 'ALLEY' / 'KEMPER' further east; recorded as Lindsay Alley throughout; it runs off both the west and east edges, crossing all four streets. The three north-south 20 ft alleys run from Wayne south off the bottom edge: x~1120 is labelled 'PRESLEY' (Burbank-Wilkinson block) and '...Y ALLEY' (Morgan-Burbank block), x~2065 is 'CLIFTON' (Burbank-Wilkinson), x~3002 is 'FARAN' (Burbank-Wilkinson); in the Wayne-Morgan blocks each is labelled only 'ALLEY'. Each is recorded under its southern name along its full length; they do not continue north of Wayne. Burbank between Kenton and Concord is printed '(NOT OPEN)' (50 ft, drawn with dashed block lines); the Concord/Burbank point is that platted, unopened junction, and Burbank does not continue east of Concord. Wilkinson is printed 'WILKINSON (NOT OPEN)' in the May-Kenton block (solid block lines); its points are recorded but the street was not open there in 1904. Morgan, Wayne and Lindsay Alley continue east of Concord onto sheet 197; Burbank and Wilkinson stop at Concord (T)."
